==English==

===Etymology===
A reference to the literal bottom line of an income statement or other accounting record.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-bottom line.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable|business}} The final [[balance]]; the amount of [[money]] or [[profit]] left after everything has been tallied.
#* {{seeCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} The [[summary]] or [[result]]; the most important information.
#: {{syn|en|upshot|net-net}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''bottom line''' is that there simply are not enough hours in the day to finish all there is to do.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1980|author=w:Teena Marie|album=Irons in the Fire|title=I Need Your Lovin’|passage=I need your lovin' and that's the '''bottom line'''&nbsp;/ I need your lovin' or just a little time}}
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=1988
|author=w:Richard Nixon
|chapter=The Superpowers
|title=1999: Victory Without War
|url=https://archive.org/details/1999victorywitho00nixo/
|publisher=w:Simon and Schuster
|ISBN=0-671-62712-0
|LCCN=88-4547
|OCLC=17321859
|page=38
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/1999victorywitho00nixo/page/38/
|text=When Gorbachev totals up the balance sheet of Soviet strengths and weaknesses, the '''bottom line''' is not encouraging. Moscow has put itself into a unique historical position: It does not have a single ally among the major powers of the world.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Phil McNulty|title='England horribly fallible in defence' against Kosovo in Euro 2020 qualifying|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/49657650|date=10 September 2019|text=The '''bottom line''' is this&nbsp;- England have little or no chance of beating quality international sides if they defend as shoddily and carelessly as this, if they give possession away as cheaply as this and are as easy to get at as Kosovo made it look.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 July 26|author=Stefanie Foster|title=Rebuild trust or it's game over|journal=RAIL|issue=988|page=3|text=But the '''bottom line''' is that passengers want to see staff at a station and be able to find them easily.}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}
# A minimum acceptable result from a negotiation.
#: ''My '''bottom line''' for this job is $125,000; any less and I'll walk away.''
#:: {{synonyms|en|BATNA|reservation price}}

